# Hot-path performance

Ashenwake combat must stay bounded under pack + overlapping-AoE stress. Do not reintroduce per-frame scans, unique materials, or unbounded `new()`/`queue_free()` on hit/tick/FX paths.

## Pools and lifecycle

- Pool repeating FX, labels, and projectiles. Warm up in `Arena._ready`. Steal oldest when full; never grow unbounded.
- Prune with `is_instance_valid` before reuse. Arena reload must not leave the static pool pointing at freed nodes.
- Cap spawn rate (token bucket). Dropping a visual must not drop damage, status, or meter.

## Geometry and materials

- Build CPU meshes once (spawn / hop reveal). Do not `SurfaceTool.commit()` every `_process`.
- Snapshot NPC endpoints. Follow only `GameSession.active_unit` origins, and only at ~10 Hz.
- Share `ShaderMaterial` / particle resources. Cache split-color combat-text materials; never one unique material per label.

## Simulation and queries

- Never linearly scan `ArenaState.units` on a hot path. Use typed `ArenaState` spatial helpers.
- Match the gameplay shape: radius, cone, segment/capsule, and wall queries use a spatial broad phase followed by exact geometry. Preserve team, structure, line-of-sight, origin, width, endpoint, and boundary semantics; a radius approximation is not parity.
- Batch same-source same-window procs and keep summed damage. Time-slice AoE pulses and chain flushes with an explicit per-physics-frame budget.
- One shared runner ticks many instances, including repeated proc/chain drains. Do not give every unit, zone, label, bolt, or meter row its own `_process` or duplicate global drain.
- Refresh zone/wall auras at a bounded cadence and distribute work across frames. Immediate enter/exit behavior remains correct where gameplay depends on it.

## HUD and combat text

- Index live combat text (periodic / cast / queue). Do not linear-scan `_live` on every hit.
- Use dirty/versioned HUD sections. Keep health/cast animation responsive; refresh buffs, target frames, ability art, and meters only when changed or at a bounded cadence (normally no faster than ~10 Hz).

## Evidence and acceptance

- Capture before/after profiler evidence for frame/script time, object/material counts, and orphan nodes. Pool, cache materials, or redesign only where the data shows sustained churn or cost.
- Preserve established bounded designs unless profiling proves they are the bottleneck. Do not replace working pooling/budget code speculatively.
- Ask what the 60-dummy × overlapping-AoE cost is. If it is `O(zones × units × hops)` per tick or allocates per hit, batch, index, pool, or budget it before shipping.
- Combat/VFX/HUD hot-path changes pass the local 60-dummy manual gate with overlapping AoEs, lightning, walls/projectiles, HUD, and damage numbers active: unchanged behavior, stable object counts, equal-or-better frame/script time.

Reference implementations: the bounded pools/budgets in `thunder_wave_fx.gd`, `damage_number.gd`, and `ground_aoe_fx.gd`, plus typed spatial helpers owned by `arena_state.gd`.
